[role="help"]
If the client is unable to pull from the server, it can register by having the server push to it instead.
The group link for server to client should be set to push.

ifdef::pro[]
From the Manage Nodes screen on the server, click on the *Add* button and then select *Remote*.

image::images/manage/manage-nodes-push-registration.png[role="help"]

endif::pro[]

You can open registration from the command line with the following command:

`bin/symadmin open-registration --engine <engine name> <node group> <external id> <sync url>`

The <node group>, <external id>, and <sync url> should match the `group.id`, `external.id`, and `sync.url` in the registering node's <<Node Properties File>>.

[IMPORTANT]
====
The push job skips nodes that have no batches to send, which includes a node waiting for push registration.
The registration stays open and nothing is logged.
Set these parameters on the server before opening registration:

* `sync.use.ready.queues=false`
* `push.thread.per.server.count` should be at least the number of nodes the server pushes to multiplied by the number of queues per node.
Each node has one queue per distinct channel queue (`default`, `system`, and `reload` by default).
ifdef::pro[]
SymmetricDS Pro by default also adds 20 additional reload queues. So for example, one push node with default settings has 23 queues and a value of `push.thread.per.server.count=30` will correctly push registration.
endif::pro[]
====
